# Minecraft Version(s): 26.3
## New: Companion Merl
- *"Can you stay with me?"*, *"give me a hand"* or *"keep me company"*: Merl stays by your side (only you see her) and follows you around, flying along when you glide or fly
- She dresses for the situation: a gold helmet and fire resistance in the Nether, a pumpkin in the End, a turtle helmet and trident underwater, sword and shield when monsters are near, a pickaxe and torch underground, a fishing rod, a hoe or your building block when you're fishing, farming or building, warm clothes in the snow, and a golden apple ready when you're hurt
- She warns you about creepers, reminds you when you're hurt, hungry or night is falling, and chats with you now and then
- *"You can go now"* or *"stop following me"* sends her home. While she guides you somewhere, the guide takes over, and she comes back afterwards
- Server admins can turn her off with `companion` in the config

## New: Weather forecast
- *"Will it rain?"*, *"when does the storm end?"* or *"weather forecast"*: Merl reads the world's real weather timers and tells you when rain or thunder starts or stops, in real minutes and as an in-game time
- With Nice Actions installed, she uses its calendar: *"tomorrow, 7:17 AM"* or *"Tuesday, January 9, 7:00 PM"*, and *"what's the date?"* gives the weekday, date, season and time
- *"When is the next full moon?"*: tonight's moon and the nights until the next full and new moon
- A slower day, like a 40-minute daylight cycle, is taken into account

## New: Trivia quiz
- *"Quiz me"*: over 250 hand-written Minecraft questions with clickable answers
- Right answers, streaks and your best streak are saved; *"quiz leaderboard"* shows the top 10

## New: Hide and seek
- *"Let's play hide and seek"*: Merl hides somewhere nearby (only you see her), and the action bar tells you warmer or colder
- Walk up and look her in the eyes to find her. Your fastest time is saved. *"I give up"* and she shows you where she was

## New: Biome collection and advancement coach
- *"Which biomes haven't I visited?"*: your Adventuring Time progress, the biomes you still need, and the closest one with **[Guide me]**
- *"What advancement should I get?"*: the advancement you're closest to, what's still missing, and a tip. *"What's left for Monster Hunter?"* works for any advancement by name
- Each new feature can be turned off in the config: `weatherForecast`, `trivia`, `hideAndSeek`, `biomeCollection`, `advancementCoach`

## Merl has a lot more to say
- Every kind of message Merl has now comes in at least 200 versions, almost 80,000 lines in total: answers, greetings, reminders, server info, coordinates, her moods, favorites, stories and songs, so she repeats herself far less

## Guide
- **Merl is there right away:** while she's still finding the way (a big base can take a few seconds) or when there's no way, she waits next to you and follows you, instead of not showing up at all
- Out of caves and bases, the path search heads for the surface sooner
- Magma blocks count as walkable

## Merl's voice
- Merl now speaks with a high-pitched villager "hmm" instead of the egg plop
- The sound settings became one switch in the config: `messageSounds` (on by default). If you had turned the sound off, it stays off

## Recipes
- *"How do I craft …?"* now answers with just the recipe, without wiki pages underneath (an item without a recipe still gets the wiki)
